  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Sir George Bullough was a British heir to a Lancashire textile-machinery fortune. Educated at Harrow, he inherited a share of Howard and Bullough and the island of Rum from his father in 1891. He commissioned Kinloch Castle as an elaborate sporting retreat, bringing the family’s industrial wealth to the Inner Hebrides.",
    "html": "<p>Sir George Bullough was a British heir to a Lancashire textile-machinery fortune. Educated at Harrow, he inherited a share of Howard and Bullough and the island of Rum from his father in 1891. He commissioned Kinloch Castle as an elaborate sporting retreat, bringing the family’s industrial wealth to the Inner Hebrides.</p>\r\n",
